From: Batman <yellow.winson@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] batman: enable the memory cgroup controller on Pi 3A+/3B+ (#209)

Drop cgroup_disable=memory from the bcm2710-rpi-3-b-plus /chosen bootargs (the DTB the
Pi 3A+ boots) by re-declaring bootargs at the end of the board file. Same reasoning as
999-batman-enable-memcg.patch for the Pi 4. DTB-only: kernel binary and vermagic unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Batman <yellow.winson@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b-plus.dts	2026-10-01 23:27:31.041892346 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b-plus.dts	2026-10-01 23:27:31.046152516 +0800
@@ -293,3 +293,16 @@
 		eth_max_speed = <&eth_phy>,"max-speed:0";
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Batman (#209 S4-6): enable the memory cgroup controller on the Pi 3A+/3B+ so docker can enforce
+ * --memory and batman-autocommit's docker gate can pass. Upstream 950-1349 removed the RPi kernel's
+ * implicit cgroup_disable, so the DT bootargs token (inherited here from bcm271x-rpi-bt.dtsi) is the
+ * only thing turning memcg off. Re-declare /chosen/bootargs at the END of this board file (dtc keeps
+ * the last definition) instead of editing the shared .dtsi, so no other board's DTB changes.
+ */
+/ {
+	chosen {
+		bootargs = "coherent_pool=1M 8250.nr_uarts=1 snd_bcm2835.enable_headphones=0";
+	};
+};
